| Hardcoded `DB_PATH`, `LOG_FILE`, `DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_USER`, `DB_PASS` | All six pulled from env vars (`METRICS_DB_PATH`, `LOG_FILE_PATH`, `DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_USER`, `DB_PASS`) with sensible defaults |
| SQL injection via `"INSERT ... VALUES ('%s', %d)" % (...)` | Parameterized queries with `?` placeholders via `executemany` |
| One 100-line `proc_data()` function | 8 focused functions in ETL phases — `parse_log_file` (Extract), `compute_error_summary` / `compute_api_latency` / `count_active_sessions` (Transform), `load_to_db` / `generate_html` / `write_report` (Load), `run_pipeline` (orchestration) |
| Fragile `line.split(" ")` parsing | Three compiled regex patterns with named groups (`LINE_RE`, `USER_RE`, `API_RE`) |
| No type hints, no docstrings | Full type hints (`re.Pattern[str]`, `dict[str, int]`, etc.) and docstrings on every public function |
| Bare `open()` without context manager, bare `connect()` without `finally` | `with` blocks for file I/O and `try/finally` for DB connection |
| No HTML output escaping | `&` → `&amp;`, `<` → `&lt;` in user-facing strings |
| Original file left in place | New file `pipeline_refactored.py` (the original `pipeline.py` is untouched) |

